---
import Answer from "../../components/Answer.astro";
import DataNote from "../../components/DataNote.astro";
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import { catalog } from "../../lib/catalog.js";
import { metaDescription } from "../../lib/format.js";
import { webAppLd } from "../../lib/schema.js";

const sentences = [
  "StoveRatings' planning range is heated square feet times a BTU-per-hour factor that depends on the band you pick.",
  "For 2,000 square feet in the moderate band, 2,000 times 30 is 60,000 BTU/hr and 2,000 times 45 is 90,000 BTU/hr.",
  "Those factors are ours, for an 8-foot ceiling, and they are not EPA figures or a room-by-room heat-loss calculation.",
];
const description = metaDescription(sentences);
const factors = [
  ["Mild", "Winters usually stay above about 20°F", "20", "30"],
  ["Moderate", "Winters often fall between 0°F and 20°F", "30", "45"],
  ["Cold", "Winters often fall below 0°F", "45", "60"],
  ["Severe", "Long stretches well below 0°F, or a drafty building", "60", "75"],
];
---

<Base title="Stove size calculator" description={description} breadcrumbs={[{ href: "/", label: "Home" }, { href: "/tools/stove-size-calculator/", label: "Stove size calculator" }]} jsonLd={[webAppLd("Stove size calculator", description, "/tools/stove-size-calculator/")]}>
  <div class="wrap">
    <h1>Stove size calculator</h1>
    <Answer sentences={sentences} />
    <form id="size-form">
      <div class="filters">
        <label>Heated floor area (square feet)
          <input id="sqft" name="sqft" type="number" min="1" max="20000" value="2000" inputmode="numeric" required>
        </label>
        <label>Planning band
          <select id="climate" name="climate">
            <option value="mild">Mild, 20–30 BTU/hr per sq ft</option>
            <option value="moderate" selected>Moderate, 30–45 BTU/hr per sq ft</option>
            <option value="cold">Cold, 45–60 BTU/hr per sq ft</option>
            <option value="severe">Severe, 60–75 BTU/hr per sq ft</option>
          </select>
        </label>
      </div>
      <button type="submit">Calculate</button>
    </form>
    <p id="size-result" class="result" aria-live="polite">2,000 sq ft × 30 = 60,000 BTU/hr, and 2,000 sq ft × 45 = 90,000 BTU/hr. That is StoveRatings' planning range for this band, not an EPA figure.</p>
    <h2>The factors</h2>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table>
        <caption>StoveRatings planning factors, BTU per hour per square foot of heated floor</caption>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Band</th>
            <th scope="col">When we mean it</th>
            <th scope="col" class="num">Low factor</th>
            <th scope="col" class="num">High factor</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {factors.map((row) => (
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">{row[0]}</th>
              <td>{row[1]}</td>
              <td class="num">{row[2]}</td>
              <td class="num">{row[3]}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>Formula: low BTU/hr = square feet × low factor. High BTU/hr = square feet × high factor. Compare a result with the heat-output range EPA listed for a model, which is a lab range, not the heat that will arrive in the room. The EPA snapshot date is {catalog.meta.snapshotDate}.</p>
    <p>Use the <a href="/">finder</a> to see those EPA heat-output ranges. The <a href="/tools/heating-cost-calculator/">heating cost calculator</a> can turn this BTU-per-hour result into a season cost. You enter the hours. Those hours are not part of this formula.</p>
    <DataNote items={["This sketch assumes the stove heats the whole floor area and the ceiling is about 8 feet.", "Insulation, layout, and a tall room change the result. A heat-loss calculation is the right tool for a purchase.", "StoveRatings does not sell stoves and does not set these factors from EPA data."]} />
  </div>
</Base>
<script src="/scripts/calculator.js" defer></script>
